  <body>
    <front><contents /></front>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the TTIOReader protocol
      </heading>
      <protocol name="TTIOReader">
        <declared>TTIOReader.h</declared>
        <conform>NSObject</conform>
        <desc>
          <p>
            <em>Declared In:</em> Import/TTIOReader.h
          </p>
          <p>
            Uniform importer interface: parse one or more
            sources into a normalized
            <code>TTIOImportedDataset</code> draft. Per-format
            adapters (OT5/OT6) implement this protocol and the
            importer registry (OT7) dispatches through it.
          </p>
          <p>
            <code>inputs[0]</code> is the primary source; extra
            entries carry secondary files (e.g. an imzML
            <code>.ibd</code>). <code>options</code> carries
            format-specific knobs (name, sample,
            region, reference, ms2, ibd, encoding).
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Cross-language equivalents:</strong>
            <br /> Python: <code>ttio.importers.Reader</code>
            <br /> Java:
            <code>global.thalion.ttio.importers.Reader</code>
          </p>
        </desc>
        <method type="TTIOImportedDataset*">
          <sel>readInputs:</sel>
          <arg type="NSArray&lt;NSString*&gt;*">inputs</arg>
          <sel>options:</sel>
          <arg type="NSDictionary&lt;NSString*,id&gt;*">options</arg>
          <sel>progress:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOProgressBlock">progress</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError*_Nullable*_Nullable">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Parses <code><var>inputs</var></code> into a
            <code>TTIOImportedDataset</code> draft. @param
            <var>inputs</var> Source paths;
            <code>inputs[0]</code> is the primary source. @param
            <var>options</var> Format-specific knobs. @param
            <var>progress</var> Optional <var>progress</var>
            callback. @param <var>error</var> Out
            <var>error</var> on failure. @return The
            imported-dataset draft, or
            <code>nil</code> on failure.
          </desc>
        </method>
      </protocol>
    </chapter>
  </body>
</gsdoc>
